{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nCommit 7fa8102477 (2026-08-08, \"Bound malformed overlap judge calls\") bounded `judge_batch` with `output_token_limit=1024`, `structured_retry_limit=0`, `transport_attempt_limit=1`, `request_timeout_limit_s=60`. The sibling call site `judge_one` in `src/rebar/llm/overlap/judge.py` — the VOLUME site (~18 of 23 LLM calls in one measured plan review, per the module's own comment) — was not given the same bounds.\n\nMeasured consequence (local usage logs, 2026-08-06→08-11): 322 terminal `overlap-judge` failures with `finish_reason=length`, each burning 48,000 output tokens = 3 attempts (pydantic-ai `OUTPUT_RETRIES=2` default) x the 16,000 default `max_tokens` cap, ~$132 of pure waste; 20+ occurrences after the 08-08 fix landed, and 7 more reproduced during replay experiments on 2026-08-11. An overlap verdict is ~100 output tokens, so an unbounded retry ladder buys nothing.\n\n## Plan\n\nMirror `judge_batch`'s bounds onto `judge_one`'s `RunRequest` (same values, same rationale comment): `output_token_limit=1024`, `structured_retry_limit=0`, `transport_attempt_limit=1`, `request_timeout_limit_s=60`. The overlap step is advisory and already abstains on any error, so tighter bounds cannot change a review verdict — a bounded failure degrades to the same abstain as an unbounded one, at ~2% of the cost.\n\nAdd a unit test pinning the bounds on the `judge_one` request (mirroring whatever pins judge_batch's; if none pins judge_batch's, add both in one test module touch).\n\n## Resolution (premise refuted — not_a_bug)\n\nThe plan-review gate's G6 block was correct and the investigation confirmed it: production overlap\ntraffic flows only through `judge_batch` (already bounded by 7fa8102477); `judge_one` is test-only.\nThe 48k failures observed after 08-08 came from stale checkouts running pre-fix code — every\npost-update failure is bounded (out=1024, req=1, graceful abstain). No code change is warranted;\nthe original Acceptance Criteria are void with the premise. Evidence in the ticket comment."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786471863411374001,"uuid":"d22d9543-f671-4755-957d-ae8a3ce45d77"}